course: dictionary
lesson: 5291
title: Jungle: three meanings from context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. Jungle is a good example: it can mean a real forest, a messy place, or a place where people compete hard.
explain: Read «live mainly on African grassland and savanna, not in jungles». The word not sets jungles against grassland, so a jungle must be a forest, not open grass. Cartoons show the lion as «king of the jungle», but that is a picture, not real life.
explain: When you meet jungle, ask: does this place have trees and wild animals, or is it a messy or hard place? Then swap your meaning into the sentence. If «the garden is a jungle» still makes sense with messy, you have the right meaning.
fact: Jungle means a thick, warm, wet forest in a hot country, full of trees, plants and animals.
fact: «Jungle» came from Hindi «jangal», which means wild land.
fact: Jungles and rainforests grow near the equator, where it is hot and wet.
fact: A concrete jungle means a big city, and a jungle gym is a climbing frame on a playground.
fact: Bagheera in The Jungle Book is a black leopard.
exercise: Where do most real lions live, according to «live mainly on African grassland and savanna, not in jungles»? | *On African grassland and savanna | In the middle of the sea | In thick jungles
exercise: What does jungle mean in «The garden is a jungle»? | A warm, wet forest full of trees | *A wild, messy place that is hard to get through | A big city with tall buildings
exercise: Where does the word jungle come from? | *A Hindi word, jangal, meaning wild land | A Greek word for big city | A Latin word for tree
test: What does the phrase concrete jungle mean? | *A big city | A climbing frame on a playground | A jungle made of stone
test: Who is Bagheera in The Jungle Book? | *A black leopard | A grey elephant | A lion who lives on the savanna
exam: What context clue in «live mainly on African grassland and savanna, not in jungles» shows that jungles are different from grassland? | *The word not, which sets jungles against grassland | The word hunt | The word Africa
